Output:
## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py - Example usage of ArxivToolkit with ChatAgent showing how to search and download papers like "Attention Is All You Need"
- examples/rag/single_agent_with_hybrid_rag.py - Example of a single agent using hybrid retrieval (vector + BM25) with ChatAgent, useful for vector retrieval integration
- examples/memories/agent_memory_vector_db_example.py - Example of using vector DB memory with ChatAgent, showing vector storage and retrieval setup

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py - Implementation of ArxivToolkit providing tools for paper search and download
- camel/agents/chat_agent.py - Core ChatAgent class used to create agents with tools and memory
- camel/storages/vectordb_storages/qdrant.py (and other vector storages) - Vector DB storage implementations for vector retrieval

## Enums / Configs
- camel/types/enums.py - Contains ModelPlatformType, ModelType enums used in model and agent creation

## Tests
- test/toolkits/test_arxiv_functions.py - Tests for ArxivToolkit functions

These files collectively provide the necessary components and usage patterns to create an agent with Arxiv tools, download papers, and use vector retrieval to answer questions. The example in examples/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py is especially relevant as it shows ArxivToolkit usage with ChatAgent. The vector retrieval example in examples/memories/agent_memory_vector_db_example.py shows how to set up vector DB memory for retrieval augmented generation (RAG). The single agent example in examples/rag/single_agent_with_hybrid_rag.py shows how to combine retrieval with agent prompting.
